cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WaveSimFEM in academic research or industrial applications, please cite it as below."
title: "WaveSimFEM: Unified Guided & Surface Wave Finite Element Framework"
type: software
abstract: >-
  WaveSimFEM is an MPI-parallel finite element framework built on DOLFINx and
  PETSc for simulating elastic guided and surface waves (Lamb, Rayleigh, leaky and
  interface waves) in layered plates and halfspaces with isotropic, anisotropic
  and viscoelastic solids coupled to inviscid acoustic (pressure) fluids. It
  provides rigorously stable explicit RK4 solvers, including a coupling-inclusive
  bound for fluid-solid systems, implicit Newmark solvers, absorbing sponge
  layers, exact point sensors and 2D FFT dispersion analysis from seismic to
  ultrasonic scales.
authors:
